{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"body tracking body tracking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md","fileName":"Body Tracking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Body Tracking","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Tangible and Multimodal Interaction]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"body tracking body tracking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md","fileName":"Body Tracking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Body Tracking","heading":"Body Tracking","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Body tracking estimates the pose or motion of a user's limbs, hands, head, or full body so bodily action can become interface input. The tracked body may control virtual content directly or provide context for interpreting gesture and contact.\n\nAR makes this difficult because the body also belongs visibly to the real scene and may occlude virtual objects. Tracking range, self-occlusion, precision, latency, and the absence of markers all shape which interactions are practical.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Tangible and Multimodal Interaction","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"body tracking body tracking","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Body Tracking.md","fileName":"Body Tracking.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes",